From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anthony Fu <github@antfu.me>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 14:50:04 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] feat(app): show the pull request and its follow-ups above the
 composer

The composer's pill row showed the diff stat but not the workspace's
change request, and acting on a conflicted or failing one meant typing
the same prompt every time. The row now shows the change request (number,
state and CI, linking to the forge) next to the diff stat, and while the
agent is idle it offers follow-ups that send a prompt to it: "Resolve
conflicts" when the change request conflicts with its base, "Fix CI"
when a check failed, and "Create PR" for local changes with no change
request.

The prompts are editable, since a team with its own way to resolve
conflicts or open a pull request would otherwise type it each time. A
Quick actions settings page edits each prompt, saved on this device;
{{url}} and {{base}} are filled in when it is sent, and an empty prompt
goes back to the default.

Fork-Change: F-10
